# Corporate Trust — `(app)` Visual Direction

Before implementing or restyling `(app)` UI, read:

1. `src/components/corporate-trust/tokens.css` — shared `--auth-*` tokens
2. `src/components/corporate-trust/app-trust-tokens.css` — `.corp-trust` overrides
3. `src/components/corporate-trust/app-trust-ui.tsx` — TrustButton, TrustInput, etc.

## Must follow

- **Scope root:** `(app)/layout.tsx` wraps routes in `CorpTrustScope` (`.corp-trust`).
- **Primary accent:** indigo gradient (`--auth-primary` / `--auth-secondary`) for active nav, CTAs, links.
- **Page headers:** use `TabPageHeader` on tab/stack L3 pages.
- **Buttons/links:** prefer `TrustButton`, `TrustButtonLink`, `corp-trust-btn-*`, `corp-trust-link`.
- **Layout primitives:** keep `AppStackPage`, `AppTabScreen`, `app-panel`, `app-card` class names — styling comes from corp-trust CSS overrides.
- **Typography:** `typo-*` classes or `<Typography role="…">` — action color uses `.typography-action` inside `.corp-trust`.
- **Motion:** subtle (≈150–360ms); respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- **Reference:** `primary-nav-trust.css`, `shell-chrome-trust.css`, `tab-page-header.tsx`.

## Scope

- Apply to `(app)` routes and their components only.
- Do not extend Corporate Trust to `admin` or `(customer)` unless explicitly asked.
- Shop stack uses its own nested trust scope.
- Auth (`(auth)/`) is **not** Corporate Trust — it uses the GLIA scope (`.glia-auth`, `src/components/auth/glia/`). See `AGENTS.md`.
